WEBVTT

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.560
Wait.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.150
Yuko!

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:31.320
That Syaoran was held captive
by the one who killed your mother.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.360
What's more, he doesn't know where the man is.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.160
Tell me more of this later, witch.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.620
Everything.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.630
"Tsubasa: Tokyo Revelations"

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:03.480
<i>Where is this warmth going?</i>

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:03.480
<i>Kono nukumori wa doko e yuku no</i>

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:09.940
<i>Come tomorrow, will it be gone?</i>

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:09.940
<i>Ashita ni nareba kiete shimau no</i>

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:17.240
<i>If I match the beating of my heart to yours,</i>

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:17.240
<i>Mune no kodou wo awaseta naraba</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.660
<i>could I descend to the same depth as you?</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.660
<i>Onaji fukami e orite yukeru no</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:30.420
<i>I'll always, always be by your side</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:30.420
<i>Itsumo itsumo soba ni iru yo</i>

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:39.260
<i>no matter how far your heart wanders</i>

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:39.260
<i>Donna tooku kimi no
kokoro ga mayotte mo</i>

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:45.770
<i>As the two of us drifted along in the darkness,</i>

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:45.770
<i>Kurayami no naka ni
futari de tadayoinagara</i>

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:52.690
<i>we brought our wings together,
like innocent little birds</i>

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:52.690
<i>Mujaki na kotori no you
ni tsubasa wo yosete ita</i>

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:59.490
<i>When you're lonely, and hide behind your smile,</i>

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:59.490
<i>Samishii toki ni wa
egao ni kakureru kimi wa</i>

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.830
<i>like an unmelting blade of ice</i>

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.830
<i>Tokenai koori no yaiba</i>

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.370
<i>you lay bare my heart</i>

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.370
<i>Kono mune wo sarashite</i>

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.250
<i>with your embrace</i>

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.250
<i>Dakishimeru</i>

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.350
It's no use.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.850
What do you mean?

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.060
His eyeball has been gouged out.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.650
Typically, it wouldn't be
surprising if he went into shock.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.530
On top of that, we don't have enough medicine.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.860
What's going to happen to Fai?

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.740
Yuko! Please, Fai is going to die! Yuko!

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.790
No, don't.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.870
Fai!

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.840
As long as I'm alive,
Syaoran-kun's magic will also be viable.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.170
Even half of my magic is too great.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.220
He will become unstoppable.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.180
Who told you to resign yourself that way?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.570
No, Kurogane!

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.110
I'm sorry.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.580
Witch, is there any way to keep him from dying?

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.040
Yes.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.510
But if I do it, the compensation
needed would be too great.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:44.890
Almost all of the water underground is gone.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.430
It's because I showed up there.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.730
No, it's my fault.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.690
Soon after we arrived in this world,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.150
I was drawn to the power
submerged under the water...

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.990
There's something under the water here.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.030
An incredibly strong power.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.660
Subaru!

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.370
No! Kamui, you'll be caught in it, too!

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:24.050
I'm the one who drew her in, as she slept.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.140
Thus, even if what happened
afterward was meant to happen,

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:32.230
it's because of me that it
took place there, underground.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.480
Whatever it was that triggered this,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.440
the water that was lost is not coming back.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.690
You appear to have some kind of idea.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Yes.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.160
Long time no see.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.320
Yes, it is.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:51.160
I have a favor to ask. I want some water.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.670
Enough to fill the underground water tank here.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.000
I will need compensation.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:02.170
Just as when I gave you twins
the means to cross dimensions.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.800
I know.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.880
Kurogane...

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:10.180
Ask me for enough water to fill the underground tank.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:14.480
Then, in return for you asking me for Subaru's wish,

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:20.860
you will ask Subaru
to give his vampire blood to Fai.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.990
A vampire's healing abilities
are much greater than a human's.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:28.240
If Fai receives his blood, he will not die.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.370
However, preventing Fai from dying is your wish.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.710
It is not something that Fai wants.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.880
As such, you must bear the
responsibility for keeping him alive.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.380
What do I do?

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.420
You must become his game.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.470
When you give him Subaru's blood,

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.840
give him your blood along with it.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:52.220
Then, your blood will be the
only one that Fai can drink.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.390
But then, if anything
happens to Kurogane, Fai will...

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.230
He will die.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.820
All right. I will pay the price for the water.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.860
So give me your blood.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.400
Don't...

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.490
Shut up!

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.570
If you want to die that bad, I'll kill you!

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.450
Until then, stay alive.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.290
I'll do it.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.460
But Kamui...

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.500
Subaru, I don't want anyone
else to have your blood anymore.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.920
Give me your arm.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.320
Hold him down.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.910
His body is being reformed.
Naturally, it will be painful.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:55.990
Let's go. They are not going to run away.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.870
Hold the princess!

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.420
What's going to happen to his left eye?

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.550
Injuries received before
becoming a vampire do not heal.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.680
If it was gouged out, the socket will remain hollow.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.970
Vampires are not immortal.
That is only true in legends.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.100
These two are purebloods,
so their healing abilities are astonishing,

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.860
whereas those turned vampires
are just a little tougher than humans,

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.650
and they age a little more slowly.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.200
Fai was originally long-lived,
owing to his powerful magic,

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.030
so he won't change all that much.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.740
Kurogane, he has already lived
several times longer than you have.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.830
You agreed to become his game without knowing that?

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:45.040
If we had been much later, he would be dead.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.260
Besides, whatever the witch may have been thinking,

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:52.550
that thing still trusted her, and sought her help.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.760
I put my trust in that.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.640
Kurogane...

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.150
Fai!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:10.570
He's okay now. Let's allow him to rest for a bit.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:26.420
I still have some questions, but
the underground water comes first.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.550
It's the guys from the Tower!

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.420
Of all the times...

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.640
It appears your numbers have increased.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.180
Sakura's feather!

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:44.440
But Mokona couldn't sense it at all!

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.900
It's encased so as not to be detected.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.690
What's the meaning of this?

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:52.610
This feather has the quality of
protecting that which is around it.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.610
Thanks to this, the Tower didn't fall apart,

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.240
even with its exposure to the acid rain.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:00.490
There was another one here at the
Municipal Government Building, right?

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:04.960
But the Building's feather is gone.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.960
What makes you think so?

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.960
Just as you in the Building have
someone who can foresee the future in dreams,

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.880
we have a priestess who can detect abnormalities.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.220
Supposing that's true,
what is your reason for coming here,

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.470
with that feather in hand?

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.470
We'd like to make a deal.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.100
We will give this feather to the
Municipal Government Building.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.430
In exchange for...?

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:29.270
Please allow those who are
at the Tower to relocate here.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.360
There is little water remaining at the Tower.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.190
It will not last much longer.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:36.950
And, while there is water here, there is no feather.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:39.070
So, I was thinking that if the
Municipal Government Building

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.030
offers its water, and the Tower its feather,

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.080
it would be better for both of us to live here,

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.920
where the living space is much
more broad. What do you say?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.420
I am not the one to decide. I will be leaving, soon.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.170
I see.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.090
Kamui, you're planning to leave this land?

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:57.970
Yeah.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.350
In that case, it will be hard for
us to prevail over the Tower guys.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.060
They do have him, after all.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:06.350
Looks like we have no choice but to accept.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.730
That belongs to Sakura!

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.820
That's something very, very important to Sakura!

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:15.490
We've all been journeying to find it.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.990
One of us may be gone right now, but still...

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.490
Wait.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:20.620
Sakura!

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.490
When it comes to the feather, please wait.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.500
Open the bottles.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:34.840
What is this?

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.920
The bottles and this amount of water don't match!

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:43.890
This water is not sterilized,
and still has the power of nature.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.060
It is very strong.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:52.270
However, if you contaminate it,
it will end up the same way.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.190
You must put right the workings of this world itself,

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:57.530
before this water runs out.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:00.990
I have to ask, how is this thing put together?

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.030
What about you guys?

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.490
What's the deal with that
container the "feather" is in?

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.040
There is no magic or magical power in this land.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.830
There's no reason to have any
mechanism to protect against it,

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.340
and they wouldn't be able to create any.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.960
This is not from this land.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.210
I brought it with me four years ago,

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.930
when I came here from another dimension.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.470
Hello, Yuko-san. I'm sorry I haven't been in touch,

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:27.390
but I haven't had any means of
contacting you since I got here.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:31.140
That container is something
that you tracked down, isn't it?

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.230
Yes. That is my job, after all.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.820
I'm a hunter of precious
things from different worlds.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:41.610
People hire me, and there are
some things that I want for myself.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.490
I do a little of both.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:47.910
So, while my brother and I may both be hunters,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.660
what we are after is different.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.920
It's a pleasure to meet you.
You are Subaru-san, right?

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.000
Thank you for what you've
done for my brother, Seishiro.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.460
Him?!

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:06.640
You are the brother of that hunter?!

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:10.140
My brother, Seishiro, has
not yet arrived in this world,

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:14.560
so let us finish our business
here in Tokyo before then.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.520
If you please, Yuko-san...

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.480
The compensation for the water.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.820
Yeah.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:20.780
Allow me to--

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.660
I will pay it.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:24.950
Sakura?

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:27.990
Also, please tell me...

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.450
...what happened while I was asleep?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.920
Yuko, the rain here in this land really hurts.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.630
There are huge creatures here, too.
It's terribly dangerous.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:45.390
That is precisely why she is going alone

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:48.470
to procure the item from the place I told her to go.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.520
That will be her compensation.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.520
I'm sorry.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.900
I yelled at you to stop, and then...

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.950
So, please get some rest.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.700
Moko-chan, you get some rest, too.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.950
Please look after Fai-san.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:13.620
Once you've spoken up, you're not
going to change your mind, are you?

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:17.290
Then go. We will be here...

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:19.750
...until you come back.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.210
Right.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.640
Yes?

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.270
How was Seishiro-san?

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.400
He seemed to be aging at a slower rate,

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:40.150
but other than that, he was fine.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.400
He said he wanted to see you,

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.700
and that he would keep looking for you until he did.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.910
We won't let him catch up to us.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.030
We will see.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:53.120
Whoa, let's not cause a disturbance here.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.000
There are people who are waiting.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:34.830
Your name is Syaoran, too, just like him, huh?

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.370
Yeah.

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:40.500
You must have been lonesome,
all sealed up in there by yourself.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:46.130
No, since I was watching
everyone's journey, through the other me.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.420
But that must have been
that much more lonesome.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.800
I mean, Mokona and everyone
were having so much fun, right?

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.720
There were sad times, and hard times too,

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:58.730
but it must have looked really fun, too, right?

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:02.190
I'm sure you must have
wanted to be traveling with us, huh?

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.400
You're right.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.540
Good morning, Kurogane.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.050
Don't move.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:36.910
Fai...

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:40.080
I'm sorry to have worried you, Mokona.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.460
Mokona, would you go to sleep for a while,

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.580
but leave the transmission open?

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.750
I'd like to speak to Fai one-on-one.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.210
Mm-hmm.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:51.260
Did you speak to Kurogane?

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:55.050
Yes, we talked. I said
"Good morning, Kurogane."

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.550
That is your answer?

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:01.310
At first, I was going to
address him properly by his name,

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:03.980
like Syaoran-kun, Sakura-chan, and Mokona do,

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:07.440
but seeing him get upset when I
called him things was too much fun.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:12.490
I'd never called anyone by a
nickname before him, either.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.360
It was so much fun, I didn't realize

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.950
that I'd stepped over the line that I had drawn.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.580
That's why I can't allow myself to forgive him

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.620
for choosing to keep me alive.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:28.790
If we talk, we'll just get that much closer.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:43.100
Remember this much:
your pain is the same as their pain.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:46.770
Is Sakura-chan still asleep upstairs?

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.650
No. She's outside.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.610
Thanks.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:18:00.530
You're not wearing that because you wanted to, right?

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:04.200
Even so, it can't be something you want to see.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.790
You said you were being held all this time

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.710
by the one who possesses that emblem, right?

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:09.750
Yes.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:16.880
But I don't even know what world that was.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.340
And even if I did know,

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.260
I don't have the magic to transcend dimensions,

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:22.010
so I can't take you there.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.470
You aren't to blame for that, either.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:16.280
From here on, as well,
I will cause harm to others,

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:20.320
and take things from them,
for my own self-serving reasons,

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:23.370
and I'm sure I will get what is coming to me.

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.490
Just as I have done.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:34.040
Still, even so, I want to get
back the soul that you've lost...

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:35.920
Syaoran-kun...

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:47.850
Why did you let Sakura-chan go
alone to retrieve the compensation?

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.870
It's broken.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.580
Hold on, Fai!

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:17.710
Do you mean to go to the princess?

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:19.300
What if I do?

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:21.550
Don't go. Wait here.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:27.890
She might be out there somewhere, hurt.

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:30.810
No, if she's just hurt, that's one thing,

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:35.810
but if she loses her life, she can't come back.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:39.070
The princess was prepared to accept that.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:46.240
If you knew that much, then why...?

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.830
I'm here...

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:51.500
But there aren't any more footprints.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.140
Who are you?

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:11.390
That is precisely the reason
why I believe in the princess,

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.060
who said she would return to
where we were waiting for her,

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:16.850
and wait for her.

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.730
Well I can't wait.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:25.280
If you're going to try to stop me,

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.160
we will end up fighting.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.540
Supposing...

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:35.000
Supposing you go to help her, and you get injured,

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:39.090
then Sakura-- I mean, the
princess will be even more hurt.

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:42.550
The same way you do not want the princess to be hurt.

00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:51.220
You two really are the same, aren't you?

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:06.450
Sakura!

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.200
Sakura-chan!

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:20.670
I'm sorry.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:23.880
Fai-san, I'm sorry I couldn't do anything,

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:27.430
when things were hardest for you.

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:32.220
I'm sure that even now,
things are much harder for you.

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:34.640
Sakura-chan...

00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:37.140
Even so,

00:22:37.230 --> 00:22:40.400
I'm so glad you're alive.

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:56.080
I hereby accept the compensation for the water.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:02.380
Princess Sakura, the man who
stole your memories from you

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:09.010
at the ruins in Clow Country
is named Fei Wang Reed.

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:14.810
Fei Wang's true purpose
is to scatter your memories.

00:23:14.890 --> 00:23:16.220
To what end?

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:18.180
To grant his wish.

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:23.400
There are two things that Fei Wang
needs to have his wish granted.

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:26.480
One of them is the ruins that
were buried in Clow Country,

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:29.740
and Princess Sakura, for you
to visit various other worlds,

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:32.200
in search of your memories.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:35.740
Transcending dimensions, and
occasionally, even transcending time,

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:38.620
while committing those various
spaces and times to memory.

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:42.460
Sakura was fast asleep during
the first part of our journey!

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:44.920
It's impossible for her to
remember what happened

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.750
when she was asleep!

00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:51.800
What Fei Wang wanted was not the
memories in Princess Sakura's mind.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.640
It was the memories of the vessel we call the body.

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:58.270
She is able to remember each
dimension and world with her body.

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:02.810
That is the power to change
worlds that Princess Sakura possesses.

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:07.020
For that reason, Fei Wang made
feathers of Princess Sakura's memories,

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:09.780
and dropped them into all those different dimensions.

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:13.240
In order to get you to go
on a journey to collect them,

00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:16.830
Fei Wang kidnapped Syaoran,
who knew of his plans,

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:19.700
and created another Syaoran,

00:24:19.790 --> 00:24:22.370
who would put collecting
the feathers above all else.

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:25.170
He killed Kurogane's mother,

00:24:25.250 --> 00:24:28.300
and destroyed his land.

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:30.710
How was I connected?

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:34.430
You were to leave Suwa,
become a shinobi in the Country of Japan,

00:24:34.510 --> 00:24:37.930
serve Princess Tomoyo, and
in time, depart on a journey.

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:41.640
I served Tomoyo of my own will.

00:24:41.730 --> 00:24:44.940
Yes, that's what Princess Tomoyo believes, as well.

00:24:45.020 --> 00:24:51.150
That's why she sent you off,
despite knowing Fei Wang's motives.

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:54.070
Fai, the same is true of you.

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:58.950
You now know what was set up,
and what was not, right?

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:05.960
You were gathered together

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:08.880
so that Princess Sakura could
transcend different times and spaces,

00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:12.510
and allow her to safely retain memories of them...

00:25:12.590 --> 00:25:15.840
...as companions on the journey.

00:25:15.930 --> 00:25:19.310
It is indeed true that your
meeting and traveling together

00:25:19.390 --> 00:25:21.810
was something that was orchestrated.

00:25:21.890 --> 00:25:26.520
But after that, what you chose was of your own wills.

00:25:26.610 --> 00:25:30.900
So you should choose what you
are going to do from now on, as well.

00:25:30.980 --> 00:25:36.240
I will continue the journey,
in order to find Syaoran-kun.

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:39.330
If you continue your journey to go after Syaoran,

00:25:39.410 --> 00:25:42.490
you will play right into Fei Wang's hand.

00:25:42.580 --> 00:25:45.710
Even so...

00:25:45.790 --> 00:25:47.500
...I'm going.

00:25:47.580 --> 00:25:50.790
Do you think I could come with you?

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:55.800
Right now, Syaoran-kun's
right eye is my left eye, after all.

00:25:55.880 --> 00:25:58.840
The sources of our magic will attract each other.

00:25:58.930 --> 00:26:02.010
That could come in a little handy
when looking for Syaoran-kun.

00:26:02.100 --> 00:26:05.310
Is that how you really feel, Fai-san?

00:26:05.390 --> 00:26:08.560
You aren't hiding what you really want to do?

00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:15.950
It's what I really want to do. Vi la princia.

00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:18.530
Mokona wants to journey with you, too!

00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:19.870
What about you, Kurogane?

00:26:19.950 --> 00:26:24.450
I'm going back to the Country of Japan.
That much hasn't changed.

00:26:24.540 --> 00:26:27.290
But there is something that has changed.

00:26:27.370 --> 00:26:32.880
I can make more than one promise.

00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:34.760
Kurogane-san...

00:26:35.130 --> 00:26:36.920
And you, Syaoran?

00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:41.930
There's something I want to get back.

00:26:42.010 --> 00:26:48.190
It may never return, but I
want to protect it, if I can.

00:26:51.310 --> 00:26:53.190
Very well.

00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:57.440
Well then, go on, however you wish.

00:27:01.070 --> 00:27:05.160
Thanks for treating
Sakura and the others' injuries.

00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:07.040
It wasn't a very thorough job, though.

00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:09.670
No, thank you very much.

00:27:09.750 --> 00:27:12.330
Kamui, Subaru, and Fuma, thank you, too!

00:27:12.420 --> 00:27:13.090
No big deal.

00:27:13.130 --> 00:27:15.380
I didn't really do anything.

00:27:15.460 --> 00:27:18.550
I'm sorry about the bike and the compass.

00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:20.800
It's all right. Don't worry about it.

00:27:20.890 --> 00:27:25.510
Another thing: my brother has
something just like this feather.

00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:28.640
It sounds like that could be trouble for you.

00:27:28.730 --> 00:27:31.440
So, are you sure about this?

00:27:31.520 --> 00:27:34.320
Yes. This feather will stay in this land.

00:27:53.540 --> 00:27:57.400
You're really leaving?! At least wait
until your wounds are healed better!

00:27:56.000 --> 00:28:02.090
<i>All we do is search;</i>

00:27:56.000 --> 00:28:02.090
<i>Sagashite bakari no bokutachi wa</i>

00:27:57.670 --> 00:28:02.130
We'll do what we can to return
what you've left behind here.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:08.310
<i>we're so similar, it's 
like looking in a mirror</i>

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:08.310
<i>kagami no you ni yoku niteru kara</i>

00:28:02.590 --> 00:28:05.410
The next time you guys come here, that is.

00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:14.650
<i>We just need to face each other to connect,</i>

00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:14.650
<i>mukiau dake de tsunagaru no ni</i>

00:28:10.190 --> 00:28:10.790
Yes!

00:28:14.730 --> 00:28:20.030
<i>and yet we still cannot touch</i>

00:28:14.730 --> 00:28:20.030
<i>fureau koto wa dekinai mama</i>

00:28:16.690 --> 00:28:19.400
Who was that?

00:28:19.490 --> 00:28:23.180
Was she a dream? 
Was she an illusion?

00:28:20.110 --> 00:28:26.160
<i>I've looked hard</i>

00:28:20.110 --> 00:28:26.160
<i>Me wo korashita</i>

00:28:24.870 --> 00:28:26.200
Or perhaps...

00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:32.620
<i>I've reached out my hand</i>

00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:32.620
<i>Te wo nobashita</i>

00:28:32.710 --> 00:28:38.340
<i>Tell me, I want to know, I want to know,</i>

00:28:32.710 --> 00:28:38.340
<i>Nee boku wa, boku wa shiritai</i>

00:28:38.420 --> 00:28:44.180
<i>what is it like to love?</i>

00:28:38.420 --> 00:28:44.180
<i>aisuru tte donna koto?</i>

00:28:44.260 --> 00:28:56.650
<i>When you smiled, the world
shook a little and gleamed</i>

00:28:44.260 --> 00:28:56.650
<i>Kimi ga hohoemu to sekai
wa sukoshi furuete kagayaita</i>

00:28:56.730 --> 00:29:08.330
<i>It started to move, almost
as though it were breathing</i>

00:28:56.730 --> 00:29:08.330
<i>Marude kokyuu suru
you ni ugokidashita</i>

00:29:09.990 --> 00:29:15.790
<i>Tell me, I want to know, I want to know,</i>

00:29:09.990 --> 00:29:15.790
<i>Nee boku wa, boku wa shiritai</i>

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:21.590
<i>what is it like to live?</i>

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:21.590
<i>Ikiteku tte donna koto?</i>

00:29:21.670 --> 00:29:34.060
<i>When I asked you, the world
shook a little and gleamed</i>

00:29:21.670 --> 00:29:34.060
<i>Boku ga tazuneru to sekai
wa sukoshi furuete kagayaita</i>

00:29:34.140 --> 00:29:53.120
<i>Boku ni nemuru shinjitsu wo
ima shizuka ni tokihanatsu</i>

00:29:34.140 --> 00:29:53.120
<i>The truth that rests within
me is now quietly set free</i>
